"hadiths[21]{hadithnumber,text}:"
45501,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talha that Rafiibn Ishaq
45502,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talha that Rafiibn Ishaq
45601,Yahya related to me from Malik from one of the Ansar that the Messenger of Allah
45602,Yahya related to me from Malik from one of the Ansar that the Messenger of Allah
45701,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from his paternal uncle
45702,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from his paternal uncle
45801,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Salih ibn Kaysan from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Mas'ud from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani that he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer (Salat al-Subh) for us at al-Hudaybiyyah following rain that had fallen during the night. When he finished, he turned to the people and said: ""Do you know what your Lord has said?"" They said: ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He said: ""He said: 'This morning some of My servants became believers in Me and some disbelievers. As for him who said: ""We have been given rain by the favor and mercy of Allah,"" that one is a believer in Me, a disbeliever in the stars. And as for him who said: ""We have been given rain by such-and-such a stellar configuration,"" that one is a disbeliever in Me, a believer in the stars.'"""""""
45802,"And it was narrated to me from Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw in the wall of the Qiblah a sneeze, or mucus, or phlegm, and he scraped it off."
45901,Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from A'isha
45902,Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from A'isha
46001,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar said, ""On one occasion when the people were praying subhat Quba a man came to them and said, 'A piece of Qur'an was sent down to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, last night, and he was ordered to face the Kaba, so face it.' They had been facing ash-Sham, so they turned round and faced the Kaba"
46002,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar said, ""On one occasion when the people were praying subhat Quba a man came to them and said, 'A piece of Qur'an was sent down to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, last night, and he was ordered to face the Kaba, so face it.' They had been facing ash-Sham, so they turned round and faced the Kaba"
461,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab said, ""The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, prayed towards the Baytal-Maqdis for sixteen months after arriving in Madina. Then the qibla was moved, two months before the battle of Badr"
462,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Umar ibn al-Khattab said, ""Any direction that is between east and west can be taken as a qibla if the person praying is face-on to the House"
463,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Rabah and Ubaydullah ibn Abi Abdullah Salman al-Agharr from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, ""A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque, except the Masjid al-Haram (in Makka)"
464,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Khubayb ibn Abd ar-Rahman from Hafs ibn Asim from Abu Hurayra or from Abu Said al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, ""What is between my house and my mimbar is one of the meadows of the Garden, and my mimbar is on my watering-place (al-Hawd)"
465,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr from Abbad ibn Tamim from Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Mazini that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, ""What is between my house and my mimbar is one of the meadows of the Garden"
466,"Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Umar said, ""The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, 'Do not forbid the female slaves of Allah from (going into) the mosques of Allah"
467,"Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard from Busr ibn Said that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, ""None of you women should use perfume when you are present at the isha prayer"
468,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Atika bint Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl, the wife of Umar ibn al-Khattab, used to ask Umar ibn al-Khattab for permission to go to the mosque. He would keep silent, so she would say, ""By Allah, I will go out, unless you forbid me,"" and he would not forbid her"
469,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Amra bint Abd ar-Rahman that A'isha, the wife of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, ""If the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, had seen what women do now, he would have forbidden them to go into the mosques, just as the women of the Bani Israil were forbidden."" Yahya ibn Said said that he asked Amra, ""Were the women of the Bani Israil forbidden to go into the mosques?"" and she said, ""Yes"
